.TH DIAGNOSE_NGSPICE 1 "March 2026" "IHP macOS Toolkit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diagnose_ngspice.sh \- Diagnostic tool for ngspice installations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diagnose_ngspice.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diagnose_ngspice.sh
is a diagnostic utility that checks all ngspice installations on the system
and reports their capabilities, particularly OSDI (Verilog-A) support.

The script helps identify configuration issues and verifies that the toolkit
is correctly set up for analog circuit simulation.
.SH WHAT IT CHECKS
The diagnostic script examines:
.SS Environment Variables
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
TOOLKIT_ROOT
.IP \(bu 2
PDK_ROOT
.IP \(bu 2
PDK
.IP \(bu 2
PATH configuration
.RE
.SS ngspice Installations
Searches for ngspice in:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
/usr/local/bin (Homebrew)
.IP \(bu 2
/opt/homebrew/bin (Apple Silicon Homebrew)
.IP \(bu 2
$TOOLKIT_ROOT/scripts (wrapper scripts)
.IP \(bu 2
System PATH
.RE
.SS For Each Installation
Reports:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Version number
.IP \(bu 2
Installation path
.IP \(bu 2
OSDI support status
.IP \(bu 2
Verilog-A capability
.RE
.SS Docker Status
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Docker Desktop running state
.IP \(bu 2
Container access
.IP \(bu 2
Image availability (hpretl/iic-osic-tools)
.RE
.SH USAGE
Simply run without arguments:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
diagnose_ngspice.sh
.EE
.in
.PP
The script produces a detailed report to stdout.
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.SS Example Output
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
=== ngspice Installation Diagnostic ===

Environment Variables:
  TOOLKIT_ROOT: /Users/you/Electronics/outils/ihp-macos-toolkit
  PDK_ROOT:     /Users/you/Electronics/outils/IHP-Open-PDK
  PDK:          ihp-sg13g2
  ✓ Environment configured

ngspice Installations Found:

1. /usr/local/bin/ngspice
   Version: ngspice-41
   OSDI Support: NO
   Note: Native macOS installation (Homebrew)

2. ngspice-docker (wrapper)
   Path: /Users/you/.../scripts/ngspice-docker
   OSDI Support: YES (via Docker)
   Docker Status: ✓ Running
   Image: hpretl/iic-osic-tools:latest

3. ngspice-docker-python (wrapper)
   Path: /Users/you/.../scripts/ngspice-docker-python
   OSDI Support: YES (via Docker)
   Purpose: Python/mosplot integration

Recommendations:
  ✓ Use ngspice-docker for Verilog-A models
  ✓ Use native ngspice for SPICE-only simulations
  ✓ Environment correctly configured
.EE
.in
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Diagnostic completed successfully (issues may still be reported)
.TP
.B 1
Script execution error
.SH INTERPRETING RESULTS
.SS Green Checkmarks (✓)
Indicates working configuration:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Environment variables set
.IP \(bu 2
Docker running
.IP \(bu 2
OSDI support available
.RE
.SS Red X (✗) or Warnings
Indicates issues needing attention:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Missing environment variables
.IP \(bu 2
Docker not running
.IP \(bu 2
No OSDI support found
.IP \(bu 2
Wrapper scripts not in PATH
.RE
.SH COMMON ISSUES AND FIXES
.SS Environment not configured
.PP
.B Symptom:
TOOLKIT_ROOT or PDK_ROOT not set
.PP
.B Fix:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
source $ASIC_DESIGN_ROOT/projets/env/zshrc_elec
.EE
.in
.SS Docker not running
.PP
.B Symptom:
Cannot connect to Docker daemon
.PP
.B Fix:
.RS 4
.IP 1. 3
Launch Docker Desktop
.IP 2.
Wait for whale icon to stabilize
.IP 3.
Re-run diagnostic
.RE
.SS No OSDI support
.PP
.B Symptom:
All installations show "OSDI Support: NO"
.PP
.B Fix:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Ensure Docker is running
.IP \(bu 2
Pull image:
.B docker pull hpretl/iic-osic-tools:latest
.IP \(bu 2
Verify wrappers in PATH:
.B which ngspice-docker
.RE
.SS Wrapper not found
.PP
.B Symptom:
ngspice-docker not in diagnostic output
.PP
.B Fix:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Check PATH
echo $PATH | grep toolkit

# Add to PATH if missing
export PATH="$TOOLKIT_ROOT/scripts:$PATH"
.EE
.in
.SS Multiple installations conflict
.PP
.B Symptom:
Several ngspice versions found
.PP
.B Note:
This is normal. The diagnostic helps you choose the right one:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Use
.B ngspice-docker
for OSDI/Verilog-A
.IP \(bu 2
Use native
.B ngspice
for speed (SPICE-only models)
.RE
.SH WHEN TO RUN
Run the diagnostic:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
After initial toolkit installation
.IP \(bu 2
When simulations fail with model errors
.IP \(bu 2
After system updates (macOS, Docker, Homebrew)
.IP \(bu 2
When troubleshooting environment issues
.IP \(bu 2
Before reporting bugs
.RE
.SH LIMITATIONS
The diagnostic:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Does not test actual simulation capability
.IP \(bu 2
Cannot verify PDK model integrity
.IP \(bu 2
Reports presence, not correctness
.RE
.PP
For full verification, run actual test simulations:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
cd $TOOLKIT_ROOT/snippets/03_psp103_mos
make run
.EE
.in
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $TOOLKIT_ROOT/scripts/diagnose_ngspice.sh
The diagnostic script
.TP
.I $TOOLKIT_ROOT/scripts/ngspice-docker
Wrapper checked by diagnostic
.TP
.I $TOOLKIT_ROOT/scripts/ngspice-docker-python
Python wrapper checked by diagnostic
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TOOLKIT_ROOT
Path to toolkit (checked and reported)
.TP
.B PDK_ROOT
Path to PDK (checked and reported)
.TP
.B PDK
PDK name (checked and reported)
.TP
.B PATH
Searched for ngspice installations
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ngspice-docker (1),
.BR ngspice-docker-python (1),
.BR docker (1)
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic Diagnostic
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
diagnose_ngspice.sh
.EE
.in
.SS Save Report
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
diagnose_ngspice.sh > ngspice_report.txt
.EE
.in
.SS Check After Configuration
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
source $ASIC_DESIGN_ROOT/projets/env/zshrc_elec
diagnose_ngspice.sh
.EE
.in
